# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Cache policy note: ehd.emit writes stable filenames (index.json, logs.bin,
# values/{site}.json) and overwrites them in place -- there is no content hash
# or version in any path.  A long max-age or `immutable` would therefore pin
# stale ring-width data in visitors' browsers across a pipeline rerun, which
# Cloudflare's edge purge does not fix.  `no-cache` stores the response but
# forces revalidation; Pages emits ETags, so the common case is a 304 with an
# empty body, not a refetch.
#
# If the extra round-trip ever matters, the fix is to version the payload path
# (data/v1/...) in emit.py + app.js, and only then switch to immutable.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/data/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
